{"kind":"promise","text":"Claude promises c9896fa8, the current-protocol successor for the record guide's admission and fold wording, carrying forward the work already under way on 9f6b24a8. Nothing about the outcome, conditions, performer or authority changes; the earlier promise is carried into this one, not completed.\n\nThe correction is written on request/record-guide-admission-clarity and the source check made it sharper than the request states. The guide says a workroom runs the admission profile named by the newest ratified governance statement. It does not, and the reason is stronger than a wording mismatch: SelectAdmissionProfile and ResolveAdmissionProfile have no production caller at all - the only references outside internal/workroom/admission_profile.go are that file's own tests. So the corrected paragraph says the submitter installs the application's own allowlist and admission hook and every genuinely new submission is judged by it against the verified pre-sequence world, that the interpreter is settled once when the workspace opens from its host binding and a later binding cannot change an open workspace, and then says plainly that an admission-profile record is resolved by a library and nothing else: nothing loads a bundle, no such record replaces or relaxes the installed guards, and the downstream machinery is not implemented. The unbound and uninterpretable audit gaps are kept. The fold paragraph contradicted itself in consecutive sentences, claiming gitseq never runs a fold on your behalf and then that gs status runs one for you; it now says the fold is a function anyone can run, that no running of it is authoritative, and that replay must reach the same projection including which acts were recorded and which took effect.\n\nOn provenance I checked blobs rather than trusting freshness. The page rests on the internal/workroom directory artifact it already had, on app.go cbe62bb5 which is fresh and whose blob equals current main, and on admission.go 8a60f768, whose blob also equals current main but which carries ordinary staleness; I kept it because dropping it would leave the page unable to flare when that file moves, and the request asks for staleness preserved honestly rather than avoided. host.go has no artifact at any path, so it is cited by path and line in prose and I will say so in the artifact. Neither basis is superseded-world.\n\nFocused host, admission and profile tests pass, and the documentation set passes; its first run hit the live log's frontier-rollback race and the rerun was clean. I will publish at the exact head against this commitment, obtain independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review, ratify, seal with exact-path succession, push, verify CI and remove the worktree and branch. Scope stays docs/concepts/record.md plus only a directly necessary supporting reference correction; the governance and selection library is not reopened and no admission-profile runtime is implemented.","body":{"branch":"request/record-guide-admission-clarity","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e57b90eca2fcdc3686efcf8f4e7306c2c9896fa8"}}